1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,000
Interop Playground runs real Inji issuers,
wallets and verifiers against each other,

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,500
shows every protocol message, and proves fixes
for the failures it finds.

3
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:29,000
One script brings up Inji Certify, Verify, Mimoto, eSignet
and our backend locally, digest-pinned.

4
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:38,000
Pick who plays issuer, wallet and verifier.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Combinations that cannot work are greyed out
with the reason and the gap behind it.

6
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:02,000
Issuance runs over OpenID4VCI 1.0
with a pre-authorized code.

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Each arrow is a captured HTTP exchange:

8
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:27,000
here is the credential offer, the token response
and the issued credential.

9
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:34,000
The wallet now holds the credential.

10
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:44,500
The inspector decodes it: issuer key,
selective disclosures and the holder binding.

11
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:56,000
Inji Verify creates an OpenID4VP request
with a DCQL query.

12
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:08,000
The wallet presents with a key-binding JWT,

13
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:19,000
and Verify returns the result JSON: valid.

14
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:27,000
Every run produces a pass/fail report:

15
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:34,500
issuer, wallet, verifier, format, proof type, outcome,
and the failing check when there is one.

16
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:42,000
Verification distinguishes valid, invalid,
and valid-but-expired:

17
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:49,500
the signature checks out
but the credential has expired.

18
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:58,000
A non-Inji issuer, walt.id, fails at Inji Verify.

19
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:10,000
The playground matches the failure to a known cause:
Verify requires an x5c certificate chain in the SD-JWT header.

20
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:18,000
It offers exactly one change.

21
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:30,000
One click re-runs with that change only,
and the run passes.

22
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:39,500
That is proof of the fix, not a guess.

23
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:52,000
The interop report lists every combination we ran
and its outcome.

24
00:03:52,000 --> 00:04:04,500
The gaps write-up documents the Inji defects we found,
with reproduction steps, ready to file.

25
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:12,000
Interop Playground.

26
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:19,500
Source, setup and every flow are in the README.
